; The ONE variable: `autowrap_mode` (and, on the third node,
; `autowrap_trim_flags`) on a Button.
;
; `Button::_shape` maps the mode to break flags and ORs `autowrap_flags_trim`
; onto them (`button.cpp:546-561`); the draw path then shapes the label at
; `Math::ceil(MAX(1.0f, drawable_size_remained.width))` (`:428-432`), which is
; the button's own rect less the stylebox margins. Every node below is 120px
; wide with a label far wider than that, so the mode is the whole of what
; decides the rows.
;
; `Off` overflows its box on one line — the previewer's behaviour before this,
; and the control that proves a regression is in the wrap and not the box.
; `Word` breaks on spaces, `Arbitrary` mid-word, and `NoTrim` is `Word` again
; with `autowrap_trim_flags = 0`, which keeps the edge space the default
; `BREAK_TRIM_START_EDGE_SPACES | BREAK_TRIM_END_EDGE_SPACES` removes — a
; sub-pixel-to-one-pixel shift of every centred row, and the only thing that
; separates the trim flags from the mode.
;
; No other Button-family fixture authors either key, and a Label's own autowrap
; runs through a different `_shape`, so a regression here is invisible in all
; of them.

[gd_scene format=3 uid="uid://unit_button_autowrap"]

[node name="Root" type="Control"]
